  "text": "Harbor notes\nA short document.\nMarkdown\n32\nbytes\n5\nwords\n3\nlines\nLn 3, Col 17\nHTML\n26\ncharacters\n5\nwords\n2\nparagraphs\nMenu\nExport your files to the web.\nStackEdit on\n—\nStackEdit on\n© 2013-2019 Dock5 Software Ltd.\nv5.15.4\nFAQ\nWhere is my data stored?\nIf your workspace is not synced, your files are stored inside your browser and nowhere else.\nWe recommend syncing your workspace to make sure files won’t be lost in case your browser data is cleared. Self-hosted CouchDB or GitLab backends are well suited for privacy.\nCan StackEdit access my data without telling me?\nStackEdit is a browser-based application. The access tokens issued by Google, Dropbox, GitHub… are stored in your browser and are not sent to any kind of backend or 3\nrd\nparty so your data won’t be accessed by anyone.\nFor commercial support or custom development, please\n.\nLicensed under an",
